      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-brownorum-west-kalimantan-wild-betta-fish",
      "html": "<p>Wild-caught Betta brownorum from West Kalimantan, belonging to the Betta coccina complex. IUCN Red List: Vulnerable (threatened and facing a high risk of extinction in the wild).</p><ul><li>Max size: 1.2-1.5 inches (about 3-3.8 cm)</li><li>Temperature: 75-82°F (24-28°C)</li><li>pH: 5.0-6.5</li><li>TDS: 60-100</li><li>Diet: carnivorous</li><li>Breeding: bubble nester</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-brownorum-west-kalimantan-wild-betta-fish",
      "html": "<p>West Kalimantan.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-brownorum-west-kalimantan-wild-betta-fish",
      "html": "<p>Recommended 1 pair per 5 gallons (about 19 litres).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-brownorum-west-kalimantan-wild-betta-fish",
      "html": "<p>TDS: 60-100. pH: 5.0-6.5. Temperature: 24-28°C (75-82°F).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-brownorum-west-kalimantan-wild-betta-fish",
      "html": "<p>Carnivorous. Fed on live blackworms, frozen bloodworms and pellets.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-brownorum-west-kalimantan-wild-betta-fish",
      "html": "<p>Moderately aggressive; males can be territorial when establishing breeding grounds. Because of their small size, multiple pairs can be kept as long as there is enough space and cover. Expect fin nipping.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-brownorum-west-kalimantan-wild-betta-fish",
      "html": "<p>Males are an intense red with a green iridescent spot on the body and have longer anal fins. Females have shorter finnage and less intense coloration. Spot size varies.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
